 "help.tips[0].examples[0].en": "to receive (get)",
 "help.tips[0].examples[1].en": "defective (broken)",
 "help.tips[0].check.whyEn": "erhalten is the formal word for 'receive'; kriegen means the same but is colloquial, and erhält is the wrong form after haben.",
 "help.tips[0].en.text": "At this stage two words can mean the same and still not be interchangeable. The note on the back often names the plain or colloquial equivalent; learn which one fits a formal text.",
 "help.tips[0].en.title": "Register is part of the meaning",
 "help.tips[1].examples[0].en": "The government is taking new measures.",
 "help.tips[1].examples[1].en": "He has doubts about the study.",
 "help.tips[1].check.whyEn": "The fixed pair is ein Risiko eingehen: to take a risk.",
 "help.tips[1].en.text": "eine Entscheidung treffen, Maßnahmen ergreifen, Kritik üben, Zweifel hegen, ein Risiko eingehen: the noun brings the meaning and only one verb fits it.",
 "help.tips[1].en.title": "Fixed noun + verb pairs carry formal German",
 "help.tips[2].examples[0].en": "You can object to the decision.",
 "help.tips[2].examples[1].en": "The parties reached a settlement.",
 "help.tips[2].check.whyEn": "der Vergleich is a settlement; Berufung and Einspruch keep the dispute going.",
 "help.tips[2].en.text": "der Einspruch, der Widerspruch and die Berufung are all ways of challenging a decision, at different stages; der Vergleich ends a dispute by agreement.",
 "help.tips[2].en.title": "Law words that look alike",
 "help.hookEn": "Collect the precise vocabulary of business, law, media and literature, and learn which word fits a formal text.",
 "help.introEn": "Every word this module’s exercises use, on one deck of flashcards: 362 cards, 191 of them nouns. The vocabulary of this module is precise, stylistically marked vocabulary: register pairs, legal and philosophical terms, and fixed expressions, from the themes Wirtschaft & Recht, Medien & Journalismus, Stil & Rhetorik, Literatur: Kurzgeschichte. Write the German, choose it from four options, or flip the card and rate yourself. A word you miss comes back later in the same run, and stays in your weak words until you get it right three times in a row.",
 "help.rememberEn[0]": "Never say a noun without its article, not even in your head.",
 "help.rememberEn[1]": "Miss a word? It comes back in the same run. Three correct answers in a row take it off the weak list.",
 "help.rememberEn[2]": "Verbs and adjectives have no article: type them as they stand, like \"rechtskräftig\"."
}